"""The A105 leaf extraction: one experiment type's grader inputs extracted from one text a leaf episode reads (a chunk, a
table, a window of a document read in order). The leaf episodes (``page/chunk``, ``page/table``, ``page/report``) each call
these functions from their own ``task.py``, ``credit.py`` and ``messages/internal_summary.py`` with their own pieces: what
the text is called (``text``: 'chunk', 'table', 'window'; it is the noun of every instruction and the context key of the
text), an optional sentence of their own on how their text reads (``reading``), and which window's standing records the
model is shown.

The commission names the relation the claim states (``claim_predicate``, for example binds or catalyzes), not an experiment
type: the page has not read the text. The methods offered are the types of every sheet class that lists that relation (one
word may span several classes: owner, 2026-11-22).
The leaf's model first NAMES every method the text reports (``method_request``/``method_call``: types of that class, each
shown with its plain line; an empty list when the text reports none, in which case the window is done without a record); the
unit's tool then has the model fill the form of each named type in turn (``extraction_arguments``; the decision's naming and
the tool's fills are the calls of one unit). A text that reports results of several methods gives one record per method
(owner, 2026-11-22: "Multiple methods per passage allowed"; no cap is set, the behaviour is to be watched in real runs). Code
picks, by the named value, the extraction module (``FORMS``) and, through the record's own type, the grader; the model never
picks either and never calls the grader. The model fills, with the text, the answer form derived from that kind's
grader input form plus the identity block (``literature_identity_extraction``). ``extraction_call`` checks the answer with
that module's validator (an answer that is not in the form, or a quote that is not in the text exactly once, is rejected
before any unit exists and the episode's ``decide`` asks again with the reason); ``leaf_record`` turns the valid answer into
the record of that kind (pure: the episode's own ``extract`` holds it through the custody-scoped store). Grading and judging
belong to the page's update.

The instruction texts are templates: ``{text}`` stands for the name of the text and is filled by ``extraction_instructions``.
With ``text='chunk'`` they are the chunk leaf's instructions word for word."""
